---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RelatedProducts from '../../components/RelatedProducts.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Costco Hot Dog Combo Calories (2026): Full Meal Breakdown with Drink"
  description="How many calories in a Costco hot dog combo? Full breakdown: 570 cal dog+bun, 150-200 cal soda, 720-770 total combo. How to reduce calories. Updated July 2026."
  type="article"
  publishedAt="2026-07-17"
  modifiedAt="2026-07-17"
  faqData={[
    { question: "How many calories are in a Costco hot dog combo?", answer: "A Costco hot dog combo (hot dog + bun + 20 oz soda) contains approximately 720-770 calories total. The hot dog with bun is 570 calories and the soda adds 150-200 calories." },
    { question: "How many calories in a Costco hot dog without bun and without soda?", answer: "Without the bun and soda, a Costco hot dog is approximately 360 calories — all from the frank itself. This is one of the highest protein-to-calorie ratios in fast food." },
    { question: "How many calories in a Costco hot dog with water instead of soda?", answer: "With water instead of soda, the combo drops to 570 calories (hot dog + bun). Water has zero calories, saving 150-200 calories compared to a regular fountain soda." },
    { question: "Does the Costco combo include a drink?", answer: "Yes, the $1.50 combo includes a choice of fountain soda (20 oz with free refills) or, as of 2026, a bottled water option." },
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Costco Hot Dog Combo Calories: Complete Meal Breakdown (2026)</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">How many calories are in the full Costco hot dog combo? Here's the exact breakdown from frank to bun to drink — and how to slash calories by up to 50%.</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Quick Answer -->
    <div class="not-prose rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-gradient-to-br from-red-50 to-orange-50 p-6 mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-900 mb-4">Quick Answer</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-lg p-4 text-center border border-red-100">
          <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-red-700">570</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Dog + Bun</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-lg p-4 text-center border border-red-100">
          <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-red-700">150-200</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Regular Soda</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-lg p-4 text-center border border-red-100">
          <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-red-700">720-770</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Full Combo</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-red-800">The combo with water: <strong>570 calories</strong>. The combo without bun and soda: <strong>360 calories</strong>.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">What's Included in the Combo?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The Costco hot dog combo ($1.50) includes:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 mb-4">
        <li><strong>Quarter-pound all-beef hot dog</strong> (~360 calories)</li>
        <li><strong>Soft bun</strong> (~210 calories)</li>
        <li><strong>20 oz fountain soda</strong> (~150-200 calories, depending on drink choice)</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">As of 2026, Costco also offers a <strong>bottled water option</strong> as a replacement for the fountain soda — the first drink change to the combo in over 40 years. Water has zero calories, so swapping soda for water saves 150-200 calories instantly.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Calorie Breakdown by Component</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300 text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-100">
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Component</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Calories</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">% of Combo</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 font-medium">Hot dog frank</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~360</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">47%</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 font-medium">Bun</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~210</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">27%</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 font-medium">Regular soda (20 oz)</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~150-200</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">20-28%</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-green-50 font-bold"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">Total combo (regular soda)</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~720-770</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">100%</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-green-50 font-bold"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">Total combo (water)</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~570</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">100%</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">How to Reduce Combo Calories</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
        <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-4 border border-green-200">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-green-900 mb-2">🥤 Swap Soda for Water</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-green-800">Save <strong>150-200 calories</strong>. As of 2026, Costco offers bottled water as a combo upgrade at no extra cost.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-4 border border-green-200">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-green-900 mb-2">🌭 Skip the Bun</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-green-800">Save <strong>210 calories</strong> while keeping all 24g of protein. The frank alone is 360 calories.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-4 border border-green-200">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-green-900 mb-2">💧 Water + No Bun</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-green-800">Maximum savings: <strong>360 calories total</strong>. That's 50% less than the full combo with regular soda.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-4 border border-green-200">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-green-900 mb-2">🥗 Add a Side Salad</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-green-800">Swap soda for water, add a garden salad (~80 cal). You get a more filling, nutrient-rich meal for roughly the same calories.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Combo Calories Compared to Other Fast Food Meals</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300 text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-100">
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Meal</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Calories</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Price</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Cal/$</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="bg-yellow-50 font-bold"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">Costco Hot Dog Combo</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">720-770</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$1.50</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">480-513</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">McDonald's Big Mac Meal</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~1,100</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$7.00</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">157</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">Wendy's Jr. Bacon Cheeseburger Meal</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~950</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$6.50</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">146</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">Burger King Value Meal</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~1,000</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$7.00</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">143</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">Taco Bell Crunchwrap Supreme Meal</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~850</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$5.50</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">155</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Even at 720-770 calories, the Costco combo delivers the most calories per dollar of any major fast food meal by a wide margin.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Related Resources</h2>
      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-6">
        <p class="text-blue-900 mb-3">For more details, see our other guides:</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="/hot-dog/calories/" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline text-sm font-medium">Detailed calorie breakdown</a>
          <a href="/hot-dog/nutrition/" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline text-sm font-medium">Full nutrition facts</a>
          <a href="/hot-dog/healthy/" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline text-sm font-medium">Health analysis</a>
          <a href="/tutorials/calories-without-bun/" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline text-sm font-medium">Calories without bun tutorial</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <RelatedProducts funnelStage="A" />
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
